Undefine cosmocc's `privileged` macro after the system headers.

cosmocc defines a lowercase `privileged` function-attribute macro
(`__section__(".privileged")` + no-instrument), which clashes with
mtools' `SimpleFile_t.privileged` struct field and locals (config.c,
plain_io.c, scsi_io.c). sysincludes.h is the common header every affected
file includes after the system headers, so mtools' identifier wins there.
mtools needs no code-section attribute.

--- a/sysincludes.h
+++ b/sysincludes.h
@@ -742,3 +742,6 @@
 #endif
 
 #endif
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+#undef privileged   /* cosmo attribute macro vs mtools struct field */
+#endif
